{
  "info": {
    "name": "ms-maestros · Fase 1 (identidad)",
    "description": "Flujo de ingreso del socio. Ejecutar en orden: 1 pide el desafio, 2 lo canjea por el token, 3-6 usan la sesion.\n\nEl codigo de 4 digitos NO llega por esta API: viaja por WhatsApp. En desarrollo el driver es 'log', asi que hay que leerlo con:\n\n    docker compose logs app | Select-String Desaf\n\nCopialo en la variable `codigo` de la coleccion antes de correr el Login.\n\nLas variables `token`, `refreshToken` e `otpId` se completan solas.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8099" },
    { "key": "telefono", "value": "70741828" },
    { "key": "codigo", "value": "" },
    { "key": "otpId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Salud",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/up", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["up"] }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": ["pm.test('responde 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Solicitar desafio (OTP)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"telefono\": \"{{telefono}}\"\n}" },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/otp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "auth", "otp"] },
        "description": "Responde SIEMPRE 200 con un otpId, exista o no el numero. Es deliberado: distinguir filtraria que celulares estan registrados.\n\nTras ejecutarlo, saca el codigo del log del contenedor."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('200 con envelope de exito', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(b.success).to.be.true;",
              "  pm.expect(b.error).to.be.null;",
              "});",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('otpId', b.data.otpId);",
              "console.log('otpId =', b.data.otpId);",
              "console.log('Ahora saca el codigo:  docker compose logs app | Select-String Desaf');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Iniciar sesion (login)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"otpId\": \"{{otpId}}\",\n  \"codigo\": \"{{codigo}}\",\n  \"instalacionId\": \"inst-postman\",\n  \"plataforma\": \"android\"\n}"
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "auth", "login"] },
        "description": "Canjea el desafio por un JWT emitido por Keycloak, mas el contexto del socio.\n\nPone `codigo` primero. El desafio vence a los 5 minutos, tolera 5 intentos y se consume al primer acierto."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "if (pm.response.code === 422) {",
              "  console.log('CODIGO_INVALIDO: vencido, ya usado, o mal copiado. Volve al paso 1.');",
              "}",
              "pm.test('200 con token y contexto', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(b.data.token).to.be.a('string');",
              "  pm.expect(b.data.contexto.grupoEconomico.socios).to.be.an('array');",
              "});",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', b.data.token);",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.data.refreshToken);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Mi cuenta",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }
        ],
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/mi-cuenta", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "mi-cuenta"] },
        "description": "Devuelve la persona, su grupo economico y todos los socios del grupo. El token se valida contra el JWKS del realm."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('devuelve el contexto', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(b.data.nombre).to.be.a('string');",
              "  pm.expect(b.data.grupoEconomico.socios.length).to.be.above(0);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Mi cuenta SIN token (espera 401)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/mi-cuenta", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "mi-cuenta"] },
        "description": "Comprueba que la ruta esta cerrada. Debe responder 401 con code [NO_AUTENTICADO] y data nula."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('401 NO_AUTENTICADO', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
              "  pm.expect(b.data).to.be.null;",
              "  pm.expect(b.error.code).to.deep.equal(['NO_AUTENTICADO']);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Renovar sesion (refresh)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}" },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/refresh", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "auth", "refresh"] },
        "description": "Rota el refresh: el anterior deja de servir apenas se usa este."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('entrega token nuevo', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(b.data.token).to.be.a('string');",
              "});",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', b.data.token);",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.data.refreshToken);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Cerrar sesion (logout)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}" },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/logout", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "auth", "logout"] },
        "description": "Idempotente: cerrar una sesion ya cerrada responde 200 igual. Despues de esto, el paso 5 debe dar 401."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 y envelope de exito', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().success).to.be.true;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Telefono invalido (espera 422)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"telefono\": \"123\"\n}" },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/otp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "auth", "otp"] },
        "description": "El celular debe ser movil boliviano (empieza en 6 o 7, ocho digitos). El servicio antepone +591."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('422 VALIDATION', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(422);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.type).to.equal('VALIDATION');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "8. Numero desconocido (espera 200 igual)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"telefono\": \"79999999\"\n}" },
        "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/otp", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "auth", "otp"] },
        "description": "Un celular que no existe en la replica responde EXACTAMENTE igual que uno registrado: 200 con un otpId real. No se manda WhatsApp ni se guarda nada. Compara la respuesta con la del paso 1: deben ser indistinguibles."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('indistinguible de un numero registrado', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "  pm.expect(b.success).to.be.true;",
              "  pm.expect(b.error).to.be.null;",
              "  pm.expect(b.data.otpId).to.be.a('string');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
